--TEST--
a parameter with no `@param` line in a comment that documents another one is offered a fix that inserts its `@param` line after the line of the parameter before it, `rule:tooling/doc-comment-tags-are-closed-and-checked`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Greeter
{
    /// Greets two people.
    ///
    /// @param $first the first person
    public function greet(string $first, string $sec<|>ond): string
    {
        return $first . $second;
    }
}
--REQUEST--
codeAction
--EXPECT--
7:1-7:1 quickfix add an `@param $second` line -> "    /// @param $second \n"
7:26-7:57 refactor.rewrite Put on separate lines -> "(\n        string $first,\n        string $second,\n    )"
